  "name": "Snapmaker U1 SnapSwap toolhead (ceramic-heater hotend, swapper horseshoe part-cooling outlet)",
  "provenance": "Snapmaker U1 SnapSwap toolhead with the stock ceramic-heater hotend and the swapper horseshoe part-cooling outlet. Confidence: medium (no vendor CAD or drawing exists; dimensions are photo-scaled). Sources: Snapmaker hotend product photo https://us.snapmaker.com/products/hot-end-for-snapmaker-u1 (0.4 HS, 1000 px image) scaled at 0.112 mm/px from the 25 mm heatsink face of the 2510 hotend fan (https://us.snapmaker.com/products/hot-end-cooling-fan-for-snapmaker-u1), cross-checked by the M6 nozzle hex (7 mm across flats, 8.1 across corners = 70 px) and the 0.9 mm tip land; toolhead photos https://us.snapmaker.com/products/toolhead-2-3-4-right-slot-for-snapmaker-u1 (sock and nozzle stand slightly proud of the toolhead window); 3D scan of the toolhead mount plate https://www.printables.com/model/1785621 (57 x 89 mm docking face, so the body is 57 mm wide); part-cooling duct kit photos https://us.snapmaker.com/products/part-cooling-duct-kit-for-snapmaker-u1 and https://wiki.snapmaker.com/en/snapmaker_u1/troubleshooting/part_cooling_fan&air_duct_replacement_guide (duct slides into rails under the swapper); forum photo of the swapper horseshoe outlet https://forum.snapmaker.com/t/u1-part-cooling/39888 (25 mm cutout around the sock, outlets on the front and both sides, open at the rear). Gantry: Snapmaker U1 preset extruder_clearance_height_to_rod 26 mm. Printables 1708093 is a side-panel stepper-driver fan duct, not a toolhead part, and gives no head geometry. Nozzle: land radius 0.45 mm, 38-degree half-angle cone to r 2.0 at Z=2.0, M6 nozzle hex r 4.05 to Z=2.9. Sock: 10.6 mm face at Z=2.9, 2.4 mm chamfer to a 14.7 mm square, top at Z=14 (block). Lowest body: toolhead window walls and the horseshoe outlet underside at Z=5.0 (sock face 2.9 + 2.1 mm sock protrusion from the toolhead photos), around a 25 mm open pocket; toolhead 57 x 48 mm with the docking face 24 mm in front of the nozzle; swapper 62 x 50 mm in front of the docking face, same underside; X rods from Z=26 over the swapper depth. The horseshoe is a fixed outlet, not a removable shroud, so it stays in planning (duct=false). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Derived 2026-11-14. Not calibrated.",
  "calibrated": false,
